geg@beep.mis.semi.harris.com (Greg E. Garland) writes:

> Seems like an easier solution to these polypiling, ring of conflict
> type questions would be to make these actions use up your magical
> power (although at some greatly reduced rate, relative to casting
> spells). [...] Polypiling could drain power depending on the number of
> things changing, e.g., every five items polymorphed uses up one point
> of power.

Not quite nasty enough, but here's one that is: zapping a polymorph wand
should drain a _level_! (Even the first time, when you don't know any
better!)

Now let people polypile all they want, but the game balance comes a little
more back to center, or at least polypiling gets a lot less attractive.

Comments?

